WEBVTT

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.440
<b>IMS Bank</b>

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.710
Here you go.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.950
Wow!

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.910
Fishies! Look at the fishies!

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.380
Wh-What's going on?

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.170
Huh?

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.170
A shark?!

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.050
<b>IMS Bank</b>

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.930
Huh... It's more secure than I expected.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.150
But...

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.470
Fire!

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:51.860
Shot.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:00.830
All mine!

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:03.680
What's he doing?

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.610
Is he trying to sabotage the plan?

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:07.670
Dog...

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.460
<i>In response to an increase in heinous crimes,</i>

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:22.310
<i>a new movement is picking up steam in police 
and security forces around the world.</i>

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:28.020
<i>This is the story of the services 
performed by ACTIVE in Japan.</i>

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:42.010
<b>File 9: In the Name of Logos</b>

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:46.640
It's the same one behind the attacks 
over the last few days.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.230
A bank this time?

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.870
He's becoming more aggressive.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.130
Is there a link between him and Logos?

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:54.530
Even if there were,

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:57.340
the brass is choosing to treat Logos 
as an urban legend for now,

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.210
so to save face, they won't let us do anything.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.910
We've determined the Willwear 
the perp is using.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:09.120
Evidently, it was originally developed by a 
fishing gear manufacturer for leisure use.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.180
Angling?

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:13.110
Yes, though it's been heavily modified.

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:15.570
It's equipped with basic holographic capabilities.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:17.630
It was originally intended for use as fake bait.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.890
Holographic bait? Poor fish.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:21.470
Huh?

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.430
<b>Alias
Fisherman</b>

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:23.430
"Fisherman"?

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:27.390
True, assigning code names does make it easier.

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:30.680
Yeah. Now we just have to track him down.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:34.620
Given his MO, maybe he has no ties to Logos.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:38.620
Your pranks are getting out of hand, Dog.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:39.780
Pranks?

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.520
It's all deliberate, isn't it?

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:44.240
Why else be so retro in your methods?

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.760
I prefer "simple."

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:50.560
We didn't give you the 
Willwear for playing games.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:54.250
And yet you're going around attacking 
banks and jewelry stores,

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.960
attracting unnecessary public attention.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:00.910
I'm apparently being called the "Fisherman"!

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.410
I believe we'd asked you to steal

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.600
the new freeze shot that 
Teito Labs is developing.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.140
Oh, you mean these?

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:12.490
I'm doing what I said I'd do,
so quit your whining.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:14.140
From a Logos perspective—

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:15.790
Logos is not an organization.

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:18.820
It's a bunch of loosely linked individuals 
moving in the same direction.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.820
And they're all disposable.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.660
You were the ones who said that.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:25.910
Are you going to dispose of Logos, too?

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:29.380
Mythos, you were the one who took 
over my Wear operations

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:32.120
during the Shinmei Amu incident, weren't you?

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.320
And, Bird, when I rigged the flight with a bomb,

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:38.110
you were the one who blocked my 
ransom e-mail, weren't you?

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:41.340
That incident was not intended for ransom.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.440
I believe we provided you 
with fair compensation.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:47.800
You guys may be smart,

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.600
but you lack wisdom.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.640
You see my point, don't you?

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:54.570
With Logos's power, we can do anything.

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:56.650
We can have money, women... 
Everything we want.

00:04:56.930 --> 00:05:01.360
But you guys just go around 
giving psychos free Wears,

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:04.610
and watching them self-destruct.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:07.010
Why don't you get some money from all this?

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:10.580
If anyone gets caught, you can 
just get rid of them, you know?

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.550
This is why I despise idiots.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:13.880
Huh?

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:16.940
What we need are obedient tools.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:19.460
We don't need fools with mush for brains.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:21.260
What do you mean?

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:23.590
Isn't Logos the three of us?

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:24.710
Three of us?

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:27.550
You thought you were our equal?

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:29.970
Mythos, that's enough.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:34.230
Dog, thank you for handling 
various errands until now.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:37.680
We now release you from your responsibilities.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:49.080
I told them not to kill him...

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:52.150
This is why I hate contracting the mafia.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:55.680
We had no choice. Dog had it coming.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:58.730
More importantly, we'll need to find 
a new tool for our purposes.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:08.570
Wasn't the job to take him alive?

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:09.940
That's too much work.

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:12.470
We can say he put up a fight.

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:36.000
This is bad, Governor.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:39.390
The data file is now in Inagi's hands.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:40.640
Inagi?

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:42.460
The staffer for the late 
parliamentarian Naganuma.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.560
Oh, that youngster.

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:50.000
But it's not easy to get around 
the protections on that file.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:50.840
Well, it appears the file's

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.270
been dropped at a specialized lab for analysis.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:59.310
<b>Kouki Brain Data</b>

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:55.510
As you can see,

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:59.310
there are many layers of protection
preventing it from being decrypted.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:03.310
Not to mention, the data's been put on 
magnetic tape to hinder decryption.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:07.440
It's set up so brute force methods 
will destroy the file itself.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:10.530
You're saying there's evidence of the 
governor's corruption on here?

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:16.100
It was created as insurance by a 
former aide of the governor's.

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:18.370
I'd heard of it before.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:21.050
The file came into the open after the aide's death.

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:24.710
Then you should take it to police 
HQ, not a public company.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:28.240
Until we can confirm what's on it, 
it carries no weight as evidence.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:32.230
Besides, many of the governor's 
cronies are on the police force.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:35.220
If they destroy the file before 
we crack it, that'd be the end.

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:38.180
I hate to admit it, but you're right.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:39.910
That's why I talked to you.

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:43.900
So that someone who has boots on the 
ground is aware of what's going on.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.070
So I'm your insurance?

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:48.610
I won't protest if that's your interpretation.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:51.000
If you plan to use that file as campaign leverage,

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.270
I wouldn't want you to be counting on me.

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:57.050
Decrypting the entire file and using 
its contents will take time.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:59.200
Rather than a campaign strategy,

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.040
I see it as a way to repay Naganuma-sensei.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:04.870
I see.

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:05.930
Okay.

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:09.920
Isn't there something, anything, we can do?

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:12.710
We've located the lab, 
but it's under tight security—

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:15.390
Is there no one capable of recovering it?

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:21.210
S-Someone—

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:22.030
Keep it down.

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:27.990
H-Help me!

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:29.430
Shut up.

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:31.880
Wh-Who the hell are you?

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:34.910
It's the Fisherman from the news.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:38.620
Wh-What does a criminal want 
with th-the governor?

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:41.170
I want to know where Logos's top guns are.

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:43.000
Info on how I can learn that would suffice.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:44.590
Logos...

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:46.460
That's just an Internet rumor!

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:53.000
Don't waste time with games of make-believe.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:57.260
You hooked up with Logos to crush your 
opponent in the upcoming elections.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:00.470
You set up Kobari as your patsy.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:03.060
I... I don't know anything! That's the truth!

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.050
Fine. Then die here.

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:07.620
I'm the one who negotiated with Logos.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:11.540
I'll tell you what you want to know,

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:15.360
but I have one condition.

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:19.360
Not working, huh?

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.640
We'll have to directly access the magnetic data—

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:23.340
What is it?

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.250
The Fisherman!

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:26.720
Why is he here?

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:28.250
It can't be.

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:31.850
Hello?

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:33.910
Rin, I have a situation.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:34.670
What's going on?

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:37.360
The Fisherman showed up at the lab.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:38.140
Huh?

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:40.800
Codename "Dog-kun"

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:43.430
has fired a freeze shot!

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:48.560
Easy peasy.

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:52.520
Just you wait, Bird and Mythos!

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.470
<i>The main entrance is blocked.</i>

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:02.990
<i>Please evacuate using the side exits.</i>

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:04.820
<i>This is not a drill.</i>

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:07.350
<i>We repeat, please evacuate immediately.</i>

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:07.680
Inagi-san, hurry!

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:08.640
I know!

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:09.420
<i>The main entrance is blocked.</i>

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:12.540
<i>Please evacuate using side exits.</i>

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.720
That was too easy.

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:22.470
You're Inagi, huh?

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:24.140
I'll be taking this.

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:25.140
Give it back!

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:27.310
Crap!

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:30.560
If you don't run, you'll be frozen solid—

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:33.360
Inagi-san!

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:34.610
Kuroki?

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:36.740
Oh, nice hustle.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.980
Must be hard prioritizing human lives.

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:40.860
Shut up!

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.420
See ya!

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:47.240
Inagi-san, are you hurt?

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:47.960
I'm fine.

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.110
Get him.

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:50.500
I know!

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:53.250
I'm counting on you, Kuroki.

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:56.010
He didn't hold back at all.

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:57.920
He must have a hell of a grudge.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:01.290
I've given the Fisherman a special transmitter.

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:03.010
If he succeeds, he'll contact us.

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:05.540
About that group, Logos...

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:07.600
It's true I asked them to do a job,

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:11.240
but they're the ones who 
always initiated contact.

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:12.520
I've never reached out to them.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.520
Then what should we tell him?

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.580
Don't worry. I've already taken steps.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:22.610
This is the police.

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:25.480
Pull over immediately, 
and power down your Wear.

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:27.680
Don't wanna!

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:30.040
You ass, who do you think you are?

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:35.010
A-Are you okay?

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:36.000
Of course.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:42.300
Take this!

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:45.600
Bastard...

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:53.490
That's payback.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:56.750
I'm gonna puke...

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:58.070
This is Oscar II.

00:11:58.280 --> 00:11:59.630
I want to finish this now.

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:01.150
Requesting deactivation 
of sublimation module.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:04.140
Um, well,

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:07.100
we don't have permission 
from all the agencies yet.

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:10.000
That means letting him get away for no reason!

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:14.900
Let's settle this next time!

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:16.090
You're not getting away!

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:18.130
Here's a present.

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:25.010
See ya!

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:31.470
<b>Non-Flammable Garbage</b>

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:26.920
Are you okay?

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:31.230
S-Sorry for worrying a civilian.

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:37.180
President, did you hear about this?

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:39.480
Kouki Brain Data was attacked.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:41.610
Don't you find that strange, Hinata-kun?

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:42.240
Huh?

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:46.700
I feel like it's not something the 
Fisherman we know would've done.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:48.240
Now that you mention it...

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:51.500
If only we had a way to get word to Unit 8...

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:54.500
Should I ask my sister?

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:56.180
Please get to work.

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:57.500
Oh, right.

00:12:58.570 --> 00:12:59.480
Really?

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:02.210
Yes. He knew about me and the data.

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:05.850
Maybe the Fisherman and 
the governor are linked...

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:08.660
Or, maybe he's trying to extort the governor?

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:11.830
Funasaka-san?

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:13.070
Sorry, boss.

00:13:13.070 --> 00:13:15.680
He escaped while we were getting 
permission from various agencies.

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:18.940
Ugh! If only we had more authority!

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:22.110
The tail we thought we'd removed is still active.

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:24.530
Dog's more resilient than we thought.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:27.360
More like the adults are way too incompetent.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:29.000
What about information on Dog?

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:32.580
I've erased anything about him that 
could lead back to us, but...

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:41.380
I really am awesome! This feels damn good!

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:44.090
Get your filthy hands off me!

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.900
Let go!

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:46.800
Come back to the facility.

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:48.860
Nothing good will come of running away.

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:49.720
<i>Wow!</i>

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:51.260
<i>She's totally my type!</i>

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.900
Let me go!

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:53.510
What the...

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:54.580
Huh?

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:55.810
Sorry to make you wait.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:57.640
Wh-Who are you?

00:13:57.640 --> 00:13:59.210
Why are you in a Wear?

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:00.300
I'm Dog.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:02.150
Also known as the Fisherman.

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:03.640
Fisherman?

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:05.050
Strike!

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:05.990
Hey.

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:07.780
Go out with me.

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:10.640
He took off with a girl who was 
being taken into custody?

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:11.640
Why?

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:13.290
Now an abduction's on his tab?

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:17.500
No, according to eyewitness statements, 
they left holding hands, all friendly.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:19.420
On a date? As a fugitive?

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.960
Maybe he's confident he won't get caught.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:24.350
If I'd been allowed to use the Shindenhou then,

00:14:24.350 --> 00:14:25.690
we could've arrested him.

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:28.920
We couldn't reach the governor, 
so what choice did we have?

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:29.520
Oh.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.540
Got an S1 hit on 123.

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:34.310
We know who the girl is.

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:39.900
<b>Name: Sumiyama Noriko
Birthplace: Toshima Ward, Tokyo
Occupation: Student</b>

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:38.440
Haruka-chan, track her cell.

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:39.430
On it.

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:45.100
Oh, your friends stabbed you in the back?

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:45.860
That sucks.

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:51.950
But I'm gonna get revenge on them.

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:53.940
Revenge, huh?

00:14:53.940 --> 00:14:56.430
I'd like that, too.

00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:57.140
On who?

00:14:57.140 --> 00:14:57.810
My ex.

00:14:57.810 --> 00:14:58.530
Your ex?

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:01.670
Yeah, he dumped me for another woman.

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:04.130
God, it pisses me off.

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:07.110
Unbelievable. How dare he make you cry?

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:07.910
Right?

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:09.840
Well? Will you go out with me?

00:15:10.070 --> 00:15:11.890
Are you sure you won't get caught?

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:14.990
I've got things set up in Guam, just in case.

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:16.780
If we can get there...

00:15:16.780 --> 00:15:18.560
Overseas, huh?

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:19.690
That sounds awesome!

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:21.960
I think I'd suffocate if I stayed here, anyway.

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:22.890
Right?

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:27.400
It's me.

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:29.500
Why aren't you contacting us?

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:30.650
No reason.

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:32.200
Where's the data file?

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:34.910
I want you to come get it personally, Governor.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:37.890
I'll hand it over in exchange 
for the Logos information.

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:38.990
Come alone, okay?

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:39.950
Fine.

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:41.370
Tell me where.

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:45.120
The quicksand district... Perfect.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:48.510
Sink him into the sea, along with the data.

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:50.600
The quicksand district?

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:53.490
If that girl with the Fisherman is

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:57.260
the one who turned on that cell, 
then yes, without a doubt.

00:15:57.460 --> 00:16:00.380
But why would she turn on her cell?

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:02.450
That means giving up her location.

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:04.630
Could it be an SOS? Or...

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:05.520
Or?

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:07.010
She might just be stupid.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:12.270
Easy peasy.

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:13.760
Yeah, later.

00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:16.570
Who were you talking to?

00:16:16.570 --> 00:16:17.170
My ex.

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:17.850
Gimme that!

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:21.570
Jeez, jealousy is so unattractive.

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:22.870
That's not it!

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:27.340
Oh, and I decided to patch things up with my ex,

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:29.160
so I want to get going.

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:32.300
Seriously?

00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:36.930
I can go out once it's done recharging.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.720
The other Wears are ready, too.

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:40.050
Hold back on any sorties.

00:16:40.050 --> 00:16:42.060
The governor's one-upped us.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:42.940
The governor?

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:47.520
All routes to the quicksand district 
have been blocked off.

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:49.480
We can't get permission.

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:53.320
He's trying to head us off and bury the data.

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:55.110
Isn't there something we can do?

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:56.920
Rules are rules.

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:00.140
Rather than a campaign strategy,

00:17:00.140 --> 00:17:03.020
I see it as a way to repay Naganuma-sensei.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:04.800
I see...

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:05.730
Yeah.

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:08.400
We'll sortie.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:10.500
We won't let the prefecture shut us down.

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:12.460
We have permission to fire.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:14.430
Open fire on command to neutralize the target.

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:17.470
The governor set me up.

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:19.810
Hey, can I have my cell back?

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:20.460
This way.

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:21.220
What're you doing?

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:26.730
I didn't expect us to take advantage of

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:28.110
aviation law, article 80.

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:30.320
I have the transportation 
minister's permission.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.480
The governor can't stop us now.

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:37.660
Those Unit 8 scumbags!

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:40.120
We'll reach the site in ten minutes.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.080
I'll go this time.

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:43.790
No... Kuroki-kun.

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:45.430
Roger!

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:47.020
I'll get him this time, for sure—

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:48.790
You rescue the girl.

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:49.470
Huh?

00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:53.010
The boss is going out?

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:55.260
It's been a while.

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:58.220
Vitals, all green.

00:17:58.440 --> 00:17:59.220
Lock.

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:08.400
Inner unit, begin output.

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:16.020
Oscar V, set Primavera Pantera Unit.

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:30.830
Listen. You stay here.

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:32.320
What?

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:35.590
If I get caught, you won't get off easy, either.

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:37.130
Gimme a break!

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.830
Damn it all...

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:41.910
Everyone's trying to make a fool of me.

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:45.050
I should be the one dealing with him.

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:47.310
He should still have one more freeze shot.

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:51.490
My Wear is capable of the 
highest speed in a pinch.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:52.720
Besides...

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:54.340
Inagi-san's involved?

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:56.500
I may be crossing the line, but can I ask...

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:57.280
Nope.

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:58.280
Permission granted to launch.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:18:59.240
Permission granted.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:18:59.950
Launching.

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:05.580
It's no good! He's moving too fast!

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:08.190
We have multiple casualties! 
Request immediate rescue.

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:07.850
Help!

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:10.030
We've lost eyes on the Wear!

00:19:08.550 --> 00:19:10.290
Repeat, we have multiple casualties!

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:13.340
You can come out now.

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:14.290
Hey!

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:16.930
It stops here, Fisherman.

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.140
Bastard! Where'd you take Noriko?

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:20.510
Huh?

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:22.180
She's already been taken 
into protective custody.

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:24.040
You're next.

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:28.100
Power down the Wear and give yourself up.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.380
I guess I can't run away anymore.

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:33.610
Too bad for you.

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:36.690
I've also found the data you stole.

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:39.640
You bastard!

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:41.160
Die!

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:42.160
Apprehend.

00:19:42.940 --> 00:19:45.370
Who told you about the data?

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:52.240
You...

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:00.380
Deactivate sublimation module.

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:01.260
Deactivating.

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:02.130
Deactivating.

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:03.010
Deactivating.

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:06.280
I'm not gonna get caught!

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:09.480
That's not good!

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:11.570
If push comes to shove, 
the chief's at a disadvantage!

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:13.190
Sublimation module, deactivated.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:13.810
<b>Sublimation Module</b>

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:14.900
Roger.

00:20:16.330 --> 00:20:17.860
Walking Volley!

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:22.820
I refuse to get caught!

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:37.260
I'm going to have my revenge...

00:20:37.680 --> 00:20:40.460
on them...

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:42.610
I'm gonna...

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:51.260
No!

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:52.870
That's the last freeze shot!

00:20:52.870 --> 00:20:54.370
Get out! Now!

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:00.580
Apprehend.

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:03.200
You're kidding me!

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:08.480
Nowhere left to stand...

00:21:16.570 --> 00:21:19.050
Thank you, Oscar II.

00:21:19.050 --> 00:21:20.450
You're welcome.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:22.280
So, about you and Inagi-san...

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:23.490
Leave it!

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:29.800
The Fisherman, AKA Doumoto Kakeru, 
was exposed to extreme low temperatures

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:33.100
due to his Willwear being over 
capacity at the time of the

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:35.590
freeze shot's final activation. 
He's now in a coma.

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:39.460
At least we can publicly 
confirm the existence of

00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:42.820
an organization named Logos 
that aids and abets criminals,

00:21:43.080 --> 00:21:46.830
but we don't know whether they're 
actually connected to the governor.

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:50.080
But thanks to your help, 
the data's back, safe and sound.

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:51.340
Thanks, Rin.

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:55.980
If unreasonable regulations limit 
Unit 8's effectiveness,

00:21:55.980 --> 00:21:58.800
it's the politicians' job to correct them.

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:02.960
I'll win the election in Naganuma-sensei's stead.

00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:05.230
I'll become governor.

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:12.310
<b>Student Council Room</b>

00:22:06.640 --> 00:22:09.480
Now Logos's existence is out in the open.

00:22:09.810 --> 00:22:12.310
It's only two weeks sooner than planned.

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:19.240
Well, that's within the correctable range.

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:51.910
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:50.980 --> 00:23:52.110
Ohakonyapachininko!

00:23:51.910 --> 00:24:04.910
File 10: The Invisible Conqueror

00:23:52.110 --> 00:23:53.000
It's Liko.

00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:55.280
Well, many things have been set in motion.

00:23:55.280 --> 00:23:57.040
This kiddo makes a reappearance, too!

00:23:57.040 --> 00:23:58.520
On the other hand, Unit 8's...

00:23:58.520 --> 00:24:00.290
Huh? No way! Seriously?!

00:24:00.290 --> 00:24:02.390
Next time: "The Invisible Conqueror."

00:24:02.390 --> 00:24:04.500
Japan is now a target!
